<title>GERMANY: German Jan car, van output down but exports up.</title>
<headline>German Jan car, van output down but exports up.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>German total vehicle production and export figures for January issued by the German Automobile Industry Association VDA on Thursday showed a drop in output but a rise in exports.</p>
<p>Production</p>
<p>				  January 97	   Change vs Jan 96</p>
<p>    Passenger vehicles    366,700		down 2 pct</p>
<p>    Vans			27,300		 up 9 pct</p>
<p>    Trucks up to 6 tonnes 18,500		 up 27 pct</p>
<p>    Heavy trucks	    8,800		  down 15 pct</p>
<p>    All vehicles	    394,000		down 1 pct</p>
<p>Exports</p>
<p>				  January 96	   Change vs Jan 95</p>
<p>    Passenger vehicles    224,400		up 3 pct</p>
<p>    Vans			15,800		 up 10 pct</p>
<p>    Trucks up to 6 tonnes 11,100		 up 28 pct</p>
<p>    Heavy trucks	    4,700		  down 17 pct</p>
<p>    All vehicles	    240,200		up 4 pct</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
